<newsitem itemid="109589" id="root" date="1996-10-10" xml:lang="en">
<title>UK: Tottenham year profits hit by exceptional.</title>
<headline>Tottenham year profits hit by exceptional.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>14 months to July 31, 1996</p>
<p>				    - Comparisons for year to May 1995</p>
<p>			(million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		1.2		    vs 29.8</p>
<p>Shr (pence) exc. player</p>
<p> trading/exceptional    26.4		   vs 26.3</p>
<p> Total dividend (pence) 5.0		    vs 3.0</p>
<p> Pretax		     2.91		   vs 5.35</p>
<p> Turnover		   39.10		  vs 37.34</p>
<p> Exceptional charge     7.29		   vs nil</p>
<p>Pay date		   Nov 19</p>
<p>Div registration date  Oct 29</p>
<p>NOTE - British football club Tottenham Hotspur Plc said it has changed its year end to July 31 to bring it more into line with the football season.</p>
<p>The exceptional item of 7.29 million stg is an adjustment to reduce player values contained in the balance sheet at July 31, 1996 to reflect the potential decrease in player values following an EU ruling on player contracts.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 4019</p>
